{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244690",
      "title": "A Potential Problem with Side Effects: An Infinite Loop",
      "sourceHash": "1aa7aeac945e0d4c5c71dda6339a60c3e8ff3092445febfae53b8eedfc8d8283",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "Now, it's not necessarily a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "to have a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "and to have code like this in your component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 12.783,
          "en": "but it will get a problem here and I'll show you why.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "Because, of course, now that we got the sortedPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 18.87,
          "en": "we wanna use these sortedPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "to show them on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "Specifically, it's this usage of the places component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "where instead of these dummy available places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 33.603,
          "en": "I now wanna pass my sorted available places as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "And, of course, those sorted places, as I just explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "are not available right at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 44.22,
          "en": "because this operation of getting the user's location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "will take some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "So the first app component render cycle will be finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 53.19,
          "en": "at the point of time where we have this location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.19,
          "end": 55.32,
          "en": "Therefore, we need state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.32,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "We need a state that in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "manages the available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "so the availablePlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 66.093,
          "en": "and a setAvailablePlaces updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 69.94,
          "en": "So that we start with an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "and we set this state to these sorted places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "once we have them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "So once this operation of fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "the user's location finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "and since this then triggers a new render cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "the state will be updated with those sorted places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 91.98,
          "en": "and we can pass the available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.98,
          "end": 95.00999999999999,
          "en": "to this second places component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 96.87299999999999,
          "en": "instead of the raw dummy data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 100.77000000000001,
          "en": "That looks like a good solution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.77000000000001,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "but this solution actually has a flaw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.13,
          "end": 107.58,
          "en": "because it would cause an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.58,
          "end": 109.143,
          "en": "And why is that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "Well, because we're updating the state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "and as you learned, calling such a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 121.29,
          "en": "tells React to re-execute the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.29,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "to which the state belongs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 125.193,
          "en": "so this app component in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "Now, what happens if this component function executes again?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 133.57,
          "en": "Well, we fetch the user's location again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "and then we set the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "and we execute the component function again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "and we fetch the location again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 144.15,
          "en": "and we set the state and you see where that is going.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.15,
          "end": 146.43,
          "en": "That will be an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.43,
          "end": 149.403,
          "en": "and that would crash our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "And that's therefore an example for a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 159.68,
          "en": "which when used like this causes a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "And that's where the useEffect hook comes into play",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 166.953,
          "en": "because that hook allows us to solve that problem.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}